## 3.2 Typography

Use a premium SaaS typography system.

Preferred Latin font: Inter or Geist.

Select appropriate Unicode-compatible fonts for Tamil and Sinhala and test rendering thoroughly.

Typography hierarchy:

- Display headings: 48–64px on desktop, responsive on smaller screens
- Page headings: 36–48px
- Section headings: 28–36px
- Card headings: 18–24px
- Body text: 15–16px
- Supporting text: 13–14px
- Labels: 12–14px

Use fluid typography where appropriate.

Requirements:

- Clear hierarchy
- Strong readability
- Balanced line height
- Consistent font weights
- Limited decorative text
- Responsive text wrapping
- Correct multilingual font rendering

## 3.3 Layout and spacing

Use a consistent spacing system based on 4px and 8px increments.

Recommended maximum content width: 1280px.

Use responsive containers with appropriate horizontal padding.

Desktop sections should generally have 80–112px vertical spacing, adjusted for content density and screen size.

Tablet and mobile spacing must be proportionally reduced.

Never use arbitrary margins and padding throughout the application.

## 3.4 Cards and surfaces

All card components must follow one visual language.

Preferred appearance:

- White background
- Subtle neutral border
- 12–20px border radius
- Soft shadow where useful
- 20–32px internal padding
- Clear content hierarchy
- Subtle hover transitions
- Consistent image ratios

Avoid excessive gradients, thick borders, and unnecessarily deep shadows.

## 3.5 Buttons

Build reusable button variants:

- Primary
- Secondary
- Outline
- Ghost
- Destructive
- Icon button

Support:

- Small, medium, and large sizes
- Loading state
- Disabled state
- Focus-visible state
- Icons
- Responsive sizing
- Accessible names

Primary actions should use the brand indigo color.

Maintain consistent heights, padding, border radius, and interaction behavior.

## 3.6 Forms

Create a professional SaaS form system.

Components should include:

- Text input
- Email input
- Phone input
- Password input where applicable
- Select
- Searchable select
- Multi-select
- Checkbox
- Radio group
- Textarea
- Date input where needed
- File upload where needed
- Form validation message
- Submission feedback

Requirements:

- Visible labels
- Helpful descriptions
- Inline validation
- Accessible focus states
- Disabled and loading states
- Mobile-friendly controls
- Clear success and failure feedback

Do not sacrifice usability for visual appearance.

## 3.7 Motion and interactions

Use subtle, purposeful motion.

Recommended durations: 150–300ms for ordinary UI transitions.

Examples:

- Button hover transitions
- Card hover elevation
- Dropdown animation
- Mobile navigation transitions
- Modal entrance
- Accordion expansion
- Lightweight section reveal
- Skeleton loading

Respect reduced-motion preferences.

Do not implement excessive parallax, continuous glowing effects, distracting animations, or heavy visual libraries without a clear need.

## 3.8 Icons

Use one consistent icon family, preferably Lucide.

Maintain consistent stroke weight, size, alignment, and spacing.

Avoid mixing unrelated icon styles.

## 3.9 Responsive behavior

Support:

- Small mobile: 320–374px
- Mobile: 375–767px
- Tablet: 768–1023px
- Laptop: 1024–1439px
- Desktop: 1440px and above

All pages must adapt gracefully.

No horizontal overflow, broken navigation, overlapping components, unreadable tables, or clipped content.

